IX: A Protected Dataplane Operating System for High Throughput and Low Latency (Belay et al., 2014)
Method: Separates control and data planes using a custom OS kernel.
Dataset: Synthetic network traces, Memcached.
Advantages: Delivers microsecond latency and high packet throughput.
Limitations: Requires a non-standard, custom operating system.
Research Gap: Achieving kernel bypass on standard, commodity cloud OS instances.
Possible Improvements: Implements eBPF/XDP to get kernel-bypass speeds natively on standard Linux.
